[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（英音）]
[ti:Taken for a Ride]
[00:13.84]Why did the writer not get off the bus at Woodford Green?
[00:21.52]I love travelling in the country,
[00:24.19]but I don't like losing my way.
[00:28.16]I went on an excursion recently,
[00:31.19]but my trip took me longer than I expected.
[00:36.08]'I'm going to Woodford Green,'
[00:38.35]I said to the conductor as I got on the bus,
[00:42.01]'but I don't know where it is.'
[00:45.29]'I'll tell you where to get off.'
[00:48.15]answered the conductor.
[00:51.07]I sat in the front of the bus to get a good view of the countryside.
[00:57.38]After some time, the bus stopped.
[01:01.22]Looking round, I realized with a shock that I was the only passenger left on the bus.
[01:08.92]'You'll have to get off here,'
[01:11.05]the conductor said. 'This is as far as we go.'
[01:16.45]'Is this Woodford Green?' I asked.
[01:19.92]'Oh dear,' said the conductor suddenly.
[01:25.84]'I forgot to put you off.'
[01:29.34]'It doesn't matter,' I said. 'I'll get off here.'
[01:35.12]'We're going back now,' said the conductor.
[01:39.31]'Well, in that case,
[01:41.11]I prefer to stay on the bus,' I answered.
